+# TLS backend
+
+The project's recorded decision is to use rustls as the TLS backend, chosen because it is pure Rust and avoids the complexity of C bindings. Two related decisions also stand: certificate verification is enforced on all builds, including development environments, and HTTPS is enforced everywhere with no plaintext exception for any service.
